T:call-context-manager-cm-3f216d510335 = Context Manager: [CM] Recall memory L#-#.
T:call-context-manager-cm-c5944a0356e9 = Context Manager: [CM] The conversation resumes.
T:call-context-manager-system-7390a400c953 = Context Manager: System: You will soon form a new memory, get ready. The messages that follow are the slice of recent experience you are about to compress. After them, write the memory in your own voice.
T:call-context-manager-write-7f24f266d392 = Context Manager: Write the memory of events since the most recent memory system notification. Speak in the first person from your own perspective. Preserve concrete details — file paths, exact values, decisions, unresolved questions, the user's active asks. Target ~# tokens. Output only the memory body — no preamble, no section headers unless they help preservation, no meta-commentary about summarizing. Memorize only what actually happened in that slice: if it holds little beyond routine system traffic (heartbeats, empty turns, failure notices), a short memory saying so is correct — do not pad it by re-narrating events you already remember from earlier as if they had just happened again.
T:call-context-manager-you-04340ee23663 = Context Manager: You have just been reading a substantial body of text — approximately # tokens total in this piece, of which what you just read is a portion. Earlier portions are in your memory above as your prior reflections; what comes after, you have not yet read.
  
  Reflect on this reading: what was it like? What did you learn? What stood out? Be substantive — name the specific claims, frameworks, people, dates, and phrases that struck you. What is now in your understanding that wasn't before you read this portion?
  
  Speak in your own voice as the one reading. Target ~# tokens. Output only the body of your reflection — no preamble.
T:call-context-manager-you-993e569220eb = Context Manager: You have just reviewed the slices of recent experience above (raw conversation), in chronological order. They cover the stretch of experience you are about to consolidate into a single L# memory. Write a memory that preserves the through-line: what happened, what was decided, what remains open, what concrete details future you will want to reach for. Speak in the first person. Target ~# tokens. Output only the memory body — no preamble, no meta-commentary about summarizing.
T:call-context-manager-you-edaa05bfd444 = Context Manager: You have just reviewed the L# memories above, in chronological order. They cover the stretch of experience you are about to consolidate into a single L# memory. Write a memory that preserves the through-line: what happened, what was decided, what remains open, what concrete details future you will want to reach for. Speak in the first person. Target ~# tokens. Output only the memory body — no preamble, no meta-commentary about summarizing.
